Resources for running Linux 5.15.189 on the MultiTech FaxFinder FF430 and FF830

FaxFinder FF430 specs:
- Intel IXP430 CPU (armv5t, big-endian)
- 256MB RAM
- 16MB Flash w/ RedBoot
- 2GB CF card on the IXP expansion bus, no IRQ
- 10/100 ethernet (IXP's "EthB") with Micrel PHY on MDIO 1
- Exar XR17D154 Quad UART chip on PCI "slot 13", IRQ on GPIO7
- Four 56k MT5634SMI modem modules connected to the quad UART

Working:
- Boot to command line
- CF card connected to IXP430 expansion bus in polling mode
- Ethernet
- RedBoot / FIS flash chip
- Exar PCI multiport serial chip (connected to modems)
- All four MT5634SMI modems, including simultaneous traffic
- DS1302 real-time clock

Not working:
- Pull MAC address (and maybe even IP address) from RedBoot config. This one should be easy, just need to parse /dev/mtdblock1
- Boot from internal flash. This shouldn't be hard in theory but I have not tried yet. TFTP boot works fine.

Included files:
- Kernel and crosstools-ng configurations
- Kernel patches and device tree
- A minimal /sbin/init for busybox
- The MultiTech custom Exar driver for Linux 2.4.27
- Patch to update the modern Exar driver to work with this implementation of the hardware
- Patch adding LSB-first transfers to the Linux 5.15 spi-gpio driver
- Patch allowing the DS1302 CE-inactive interval before its first access
- Notes from investigating various issues

The DS1302 is connected as a three-wire, LSB-first SPI device using
GPIO2 for SCLK, GPIO4 for bidirectional I/O, and GPIO5 for active-high
CE. The wiring was recovered from the stock kernel image. See FF430.md
for the driver quirks, modem reset requirement, and validation details.

Please submit a pull request or contact me if you have any interest in fixing the remaining issues or have gotten them working.
